IMPORT prelude

-- Chit Funds Act 1971 (Singapore) -- who may run a chit fund and use the word "chit" (ss 4, 5, 9, 18-20), the arithmetic of a sale
-- (ss 2, 24), the subscribers' voting thresholds (ss 28, 33, 41), guarantors, default and refund (ss 30, 31, 34), what happens on
-- termination (s 40(2)), the company's lending limit (s 43), the reserve fund (s 44), the revocation clock (s 14), directors and
-- holding out (ss 59, 60), and the maximum fines and terms.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CFA1971.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is
-- [40/2018] (ss 53, 54). SSO metadata: "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 4 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a subscriber, an
-- operator or a director meets. Not encoded: licence applications and conditions (s 7), fees (ss 8, 11), branches (s 10), mergers
-- (s 12), constitution changes (s 13), meetings and minutes procedure (ss 26, 27), books (s 37), transfers (ss 35, 36), the
-- financial limits left to regulations (s 42), inspection (ss 49, 50), winding up (ss 53, 54) and the regulations themselves.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Chit Funds Act 1971 -- chit funds`

§§ `4 and 9 -- only a licensed public company with $200,000`

-- s 4(1): "No chit fund business may be transacted in Singapore except by a public company which is in possession of a valid
-- licence granted under this Act by the Authority with the approval of the Minister". (2): $5,000 or 3 years or both.
-- s 2: "public company" means a company limited by shares incorporated in Singapore other than a private company.
GIVEN `is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may transact chit fund business` IF
    `is a public company` AND `holds a valid licence`

-- s 9(1): no chit fund company "may be granted or may hold a licence unless its capital, issued and paid up in cash, and
-- unimpaired by losses or otherwise, is not less than $200,000".
GIVEN `unimpaired paid-up cash capital` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the minimum capital` IF
    `unimpaired paid-up cash capital` AT LEAST 200000

§§ `5 -- the words "chit" and "chit fund"`

-- s 5(1): no person "other than a chit fund company licensed under this Act may, without the Authority's written consent" use
-- "chit" or "chit fund" or their derivatives "in any language" in its business name or in any representation. (2): "HWEI",
-- "KUTU" and "TONTINE" (and words of like meaning in any language) are deemed derivatives of "chit". (3): an association of chit
-- fund companies formed for the protection of common interests may use them. (4): $1,000 or one year or both.
-- (`savings` is not in the Act: it is a control word standing for one that does not indicate chit fund business. The catch-all
-- "any other word indicating that it transacts chit fund business" is not modelled beyond the five listed words.)
DECLARE Word IS ONE OF
    `chit`
    `chit fund`
    `hwei`
    `kutu`
    `tontine`
    `savings`

GIVEN `the word` IS A Word
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the word is restricted` IF
    CONSIDER `the word`
    WHEN `savings` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the word` IS A Word, `is a licensed chit fund company` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Authority's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an association of chit fund companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the word in a business name is an offence` IF
        `the word is restricted` `the word`
    AND (NOT `is a licensed chit fund company`)
    AND (NOT `has the Authority's written consent`)
    AND (NOT `is an association of chit fund companies`)

§§ `18 to 20 -- chit funds and schemes that only partake of their nature`

-- s 19: a scheme "based wholly on the essential terms and conditions set out in section 24", "even though it is called by any other
-- name", is deemed a chit fund. (Its alternative limb, "has all the attributes and incidents of a chit fund", is folded into
-- `based wholly on the essential terms`.) s 20(1): a scheme "not based wholly on" those terms, or "based on terms and conditions
-- inconsistent wholly or in part with" them, is "deemed only to partake of the nature of a chit fund".
-- s 20(3): ANY person who promotes or conducts, or aids, assists or takes part in, such a scheme commits an offence ($5,000 or
-- 3 years or both) -- licensed or not. (4): no right or claim under it "is ... enforceable by action in any court".
-- s 18: promoting or conducting a chit fund "otherwise than in accordance with the provisions of this Act" -- same penalty.
GIVEN `based wholly on the essential terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `has terms inconsistent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the scheme is a chit fund` IF
    `based wholly on the essential terms` AND (NOT `has terms inconsistent with them`)

GIVEN `based wholly on the essential terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `has terms inconsistent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `claims under the scheme are enforceable in court` IF
    `the scheme is a chit fund` `based wholly on the essential terms` `has terms inconsistent with them`

GIVEN `based wholly on the essential terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `has terms inconsistent with them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `run by a licensed public company` IS A BOOLEAN, `conducted in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking part in running the scheme is an offence` IF
    IF `the scheme is a chit fund` `based wholly on the essential terms` `has terms inconsistent with them`
    THEN (NOT `run by a licensed public company`) OR (NOT `conducted in accordance with the Act`)
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `2 and 24 -- the arithmetic of a sale`

-- s 2: "interest" means the amount "the subscriber agrees to forego in order to purchase the chit fund amount"; "prize" means "the
-- difference between the chit fund amount and the interest"; "rebate" means "the share of the interest payable to each
-- subscriber". s 24(1)(k): "the interest is to be distributed in equal proportion among all the subscribers".
-- s 24(1)(h): the subscriber "who offers the highest interest is to be declared the purchaser". (The commission under s 24(1)(j)
-- is a "specified sum" fixed by each agreement, so it is not modelled.)
GIVEN `the chit fund amount` IS A NUMBER, `the interest` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prize` MEANS `the chit fund amount` MINUS `the interest`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A NUMBER, `the number of subscribers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rebate` MEANS `the interest` DIVIDED BY `the number of subscribers`

-- s 24(1)(f): each subscriber may purchase the chit fund amount "once and not more often", and a declared purchaser may not bid at
-- any subsequent sale. s 39(1): the chit fund company may not bid or tender, "either directly or indirectly", at a sale of its own
-- chit fund.
GIVEN `is the chit fund company` IS A BOOLEAN, `has already been declared a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may bid at the sale` IF
    (NOT `is the chit fund company`) AND (NOT `has already been declared a purchaser`)

§§ `28, 33 and 41 -- votes of the subscribers`

-- s 28: an alteration of the agreement "may be made only at any meeting of the subscribers ... by the votes of a majority, the
-- aggregate of whose contributions is not less than three-quarters of the chit fund amount".
-- s 33(2): reduction of membership instead of substituting a defaulter needs "a majority representing not less than two-thirds of
-- the chit fund amount".
-- s 41(1): sealed tenders instead of auction need "a majority representing three-quarters of the chit fund amount", at a meeting
-- before the first sale. (INFERENCE: "representing three-quarters" is read as "at least three-quarters".)
-- "Majority" is read as more than half of the subscribers voting at the meeting (INFERENCE: the Act does not say of whom).
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `subscribers voting` IS A NUMBER, `contributions of those for` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chit fund amount` IS A NUMBER, `fraction needed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualified majority` IF
        `votes for` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `subscribers voting`
    AND `contributions of those for` AT LEAST `the chit fund amount` TIMES `fraction needed`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `subscribers voting` IS A NUMBER, `contributions of those for` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chit fund amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the alteration is carried` IF
    `a qualified majority` `votes for` `subscribers voting` `contributions of those for` `the chit fund amount` (3 DIVIDED BY 4)

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `subscribers voting` IS A NUMBER, `contributions of those for` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chit fund amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reduction of membership is carried` IF
    `a qualified majority` `votes for` `subscribers voting` `contributions of those for` `the chit fund amount` (2 DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `subscribers voting` IS A NUMBER, `contributions of those for` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chit fund amount` IS A NUMBER, `before the first sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sealed tenders are adopted` IF
        `before the first sale`
    AND `a qualified majority` `votes for` `subscribers voting` `contributions of those for` `the chit fund amount` (3 DIVIDED BY 4)

§§ `30, 31 and 34 -- guarantors, refunds and default`

-- s 30: the purchaser must, "as a condition precedent to the payment of the prize amount", produce "at least 2 guarantors".
GIVEN `guarantors produced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prize may be paid` IF
    `guarantors produced` AT LEAST 2

-- s 31(1): if the purchaser fails to produce guarantors "within 2 weeks of the auction", the company must either (a) within 7 days
-- of the expiry of those 2 weeks declare the next highest bidder purchaser, or (b) within 2 weeks after the expiry of those 2 weeks
-- conduct a fresh sale. (2): the purchaser has the right to a refund of earlier contributions "without any deduction whatsoever";
-- (3): "within 3 weeks from the date of the auction".
GIVEN `days since the auction` IS A NUMBER, `guarantors produced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is out of time for guarantors` IF
    `days since the auction` GREATER THAN 14 AND `guarantors produced` LESS THAN 2

GIVEN `the next-highest-bidder route` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days after the auction by which the company must act` MEANS
    IF `the next-highest-bidder route` THEN 14 PLUS 7 ELSE 14 PLUS 14

GIVEN `contributions paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund for failing to produce guarantors` MEANS `contributions paid`

GIVEN `days since the auction` IS A NUMBER, `refunded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guarantor refund is overdue` IF
    (NOT `refunded`) AND `days since the auction` GREATER THAN 21

-- s 34(1): where a subscriber who has ALREADY purchased defaults, "the subscriber and his or her guarantors are liable to make
-- immediate payment ... of the aggregate of all the contributions payable by him or her to the end of the chit fund period".
-- (Contrast s 32: a defaulter who has NOT purchased may simply be replaced, with a refund less prescribed penalties.)
GIVEN `the contribution` IS A NUMBER, `instalments remaining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum immediately payable by a defaulting purchaser` MEANS `the contribution` TIMES `instalments remaining`

§§ `40(2) -- termination`

-- s 40(1): a chit fund terminates on (a) expiry of its period or a voluntary reduction under s 33; (b) the company's failure to
-- conduct it according to the Act, regulations or agreement; (c) liquidation; (d) steps to wind up; (e) revocation of the licence.
-- (2): "otherwise than by the expiry ... or by a voluntary reduction", every subscriber "who has not purchased" may (a) recover the
-- actual contributions from the company or (b) seek a court order that prize-takers keep paying into court.
DECLARE Termination IS ONE OF
    `expiry of the period`
    `voluntary reduction of membership`
    `failure to conduct the fund according to the Act`
    `liquidation of the company`
    `steps to wind up the company`
    `revocation of the licence`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Termination, `has purchased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscriber may recover contributions from the company` IF
    (NOT `has purchased`) AND
        CONSIDER `the cause`
        WHEN `expiry of the period` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `voluntary reduction of membership` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `43 -- lending`

-- s 43(1): "A chit fund company must not lend to any person other than to a subscriber who has not purchased the chit fund amount."
-- (2): the loan "must not exceed 75% of the aggregate contributions already paid by that subscriber" or another percentage set by
-- regulations (not retrieved; 75% is used). (3): such a lender is not a moneylender under the Moneylenders Act 2008.
GIVEN `is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN, `has purchased` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loan` IS A NUMBER, `contributions paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan is permitted` IF
        `is a subscriber`
    AND (NOT `has purchased`)
    AND `the loan` AT MOST `contributions paid` TIMES 75 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `44 -- reserve fund`

-- s 44(3): of the net profits, at the end of each financial year, at least (a) 5% where the reserve fund is 200% or more of paid-up
-- capital; (b) 15% where it is not less than 100% but less than 200%; (c) 30% where it is less than 100%.
GIVEN `the reserve fund` IS A NUMBER, `paid-up capital` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum transfer percentage` MEANS
    IF `the reserve fund` AT LEAST `paid-up capital` TIMES 2
    THEN 5
    ELSE
        IF `the reserve fund` AT LEAST `paid-up capital`
        THEN 15
        ELSE 30

GIVEN `the reserve fund` IS A NUMBER, `paid-up capital` IS A NUMBER, `net profit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum transfer to reserve` MEANS
    `net profit` TIMES `the minimum transfer percentage` `the reserve fund` `paid-up capital` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `14 -- revocation of a licence`

-- s 14(2): before revoking, the Authority must give written notice "specifying a date, not less than 21 days after the date of the
-- notice, upon which the revocation will take effect" and calling for cause to be shown. (4): appeal to the Minister "within 14
-- days of the receipt of the notice" of revocation, "or an extended period of time that the Minister may allow".
GIVEN `days between notice and effective date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation notice is long enough` IF
    `days between notice and effective date` AT LEAST 21

GIVEN `days since receipt of the revocation notice` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister extended time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `the Minister extended time` OR `days since receipt of the revocation notice` AT MOST 14

§§ `59 and 60 -- directors and holding out`

-- s 59(1): a director, managing director or manager who fails to comply or take all reasonable steps to secure the company's
-- compliance commits an offence ($5,000 or 3 years or both). (2): "it is a defence to prove" reasonable grounds to believe, and
-- actual belief, that "a competent and reliable person" was charged with securing compliance and in a position to do so.
-- (3): no imprisonment "unless, in the opinion of the court, the person committed the offence wilfully".
GIVEN `failed to take reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reliance on a competent person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director is guilty` IF
    `failed to take reasonable steps` AND (NOT `proved reliance on a competent person`)

GIVEN `failed to take reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reliance on a competent person` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director may be imprisoned` IF
    `the director is guilty` `failed to take reasonable steps` `proved reliance on a competent person` AND `acted wilfully`

-- s 60: where a company or firm holds itself out as a licensed chit fund company when it is not, the company or firm is guilty,
-- and every director, manager or officer (or proprietor, partner or officer) is guilty "unless he or she proves that such holding
-- out ... was made without his or her knowledge or consent". $4,000 or 2 years or both.
GIVEN `the firm held itself out as licensed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the firm is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved it was without knowledge or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of holding out` IF
    `the firm held itself out as licensed` AND (NOT `the firm is licensed`) AND (NOT `proved it was without knowledge or consent`)

§§ `Maximum penalties`

-- Fines and terms as stated in each section. s 56: contraventions "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- $5,000 (no
-- imprisonment). s 61(3): contravening the regulations -- $2,000. s 58: every prosecution needs the Public Prosecutor's consent.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed chit fund business, s 4`
    `misuse of the word chit, s 5`
    `breach of licence conditions, s 7`
    `unapproved place of business, s 10`
    `conducting a chit fund unlawfully, s 18`
    `running a scheme partaking of a chit fund, s 20`
    `failing to supply books to an inspector, s 49`
    `a contravention with no express penalty, s 56`
    `director failing to secure compliance, s 59`
    `holding out as licensed, s 60`
    `breach of the regulations, s 61`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed chit fund business, s 4` THEN 5000
    WHEN `misuse of the word chit, s 5` THEN 1000
    WHEN `breach of licence conditions, s 7` THEN 5000
    WHEN `unapproved place of business, s 10` THEN 500
    WHEN `conducting a chit fund unlawfully, s 18` THEN 5000
    WHEN `running a scheme partaking of a chit fund, s 20` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to supply books to an inspector, s 49` THEN 2000
    WHEN `a contravention with no express penalty, s 56` THEN 5000
    WHEN `director failing to secure compliance, s 59` THEN 5000
    WHEN `holding out as licensed, s 60` THEN 4000
    WHEN `breach of the regulations, s 61` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed chit fund business, s 4` THEN 3
    WHEN `misuse of the word chit, s 5` THEN 1
    WHEN `conducting a chit fund unlawfully, s 18` THEN 3
    WHEN `running a scheme partaking of a chit fund, s 20` THEN 3
    WHEN `director failing to secure compliance, s 59` THEN 3
    WHEN `holding out as licensed, s 60` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0
